.Sh CAVEATS
The Builder's capacity figures are the textbook ones: parity subtracted and
the smallest member setting the size.
RAIDZ pads a few percent on top of that, and a pool with dedup or many small
files stores less again; the dry run and
.Ql zpool list
after the fact are the truth.
.Pp
The Builder shelf reads
.Xr lsblk 8 ,
so on
.Fx
the tab and
.Fl -builder Cm disks
report the gap rather than showing an empty shelf; the spec form still
works there when the disks are named in full.
The Builder and Observe have no terminal-UI view yet; their engines are
.Fl -builder
and
.Fl -observe .
Observe names datasets, not processes.
.Pp
The Containers tab and
.Fl -containers
need an engine on the ZFS storage driver; on any other driver the layers
are files and the estate verbs do not apply.
.Pp
The GUI needs a display; the static build starts the terminal UI when asked
for the GUI and says so.
